From 997ebfa542acd82a4f3637dc44a063e259951070 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 01:38:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] settings: the Spanish of the trims, HDR10+ and measured HDR10
 settings

Every setting of Hades has English core strings and its translations in
Estuary (CGUIUtils::GetHadesString()); the three Dolby Vision settings
added for 1.0 RC3 (videoscreen.hadesdvnotrims, hadesdvfromhdr10plus and
hadesdvfromhdr10, core strings 40920 to 40925) had the English only. Their
labels and help now come from Estuary 32094 to 32099, with es_es, es_ar
and es_mx. The English text is the core's, word for word.
---
 .../resource.language.en_gb/strings.po        | 36 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../resource.language.es_ar/strings.po        | 36 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../resource.language.es_es/strings.po        | 36 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../resource.language.es_mx/strings.po        | 36 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../dialogs/GUIDialogSettingsBase.cpp         |  3 ++
 5 files changed, 147 insertions(+)

diff --git a/addons/skin.estuary/language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po b/addons/skin.estuary/language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po
index b437ad6..9c2040f 100644
--- a/addons/skin.estuary/language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po
+++ b/addons/skin.estuary/language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po
@@ -2405,3 +2405,39 @@ msgstr ""
 msgctxt "#32093"
 msgid "measured by Hades from the picture"
 msgstr ""
+
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+#. Setting label: Dolby Vision without its trims (core #40920)
+msgctxt "#32094"
+msgid "Dolby Vision: leave out the trims"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+#. Setting help: Dolby Vision without its trims (core #40921)
+msgctxt "#32095"
+msgid "Dolby Vision metadata carries the trims of the film: how the colourist mapped each scene to displays of a few given peak brightnesses (levels 2 and 8 of the metadata). The display is sent them unless this is on. Turn it on only for a display that shows Dolby Vision with washed-out blacks or wrong colours because of them, as some projectors do: it then maps each scene from its brightness range alone, as it does with metadata that has no trims. The picture that is sent does not change. Applies from the next video."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+#. Setting label: HDR10+ sent as Dolby Vision (core #40922)
+msgctxt "#32096"
+msgid "HDR10+ as Dolby Vision"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+#. Setting help: HDR10+ sent as Dolby Vision (core #40923)
+msgctxt "#32097"
+msgid "For a display that takes Dolby Vision but not HDR10+. An HDR10+ video is sent as Dolby Vision, with metadata made from its own HDR10+ metadata, scene by scene: the peak and the average brightness of each scene. The picture is the same HDR10 picture. What does not carry over from HDR10+: the tone curve and the target display that the studio chose, its saturation weight and its windows; the darkest level is taken as black, and the average is worked out from the brightness distribution that HDR10+ gives. Dolby Vision videos, HDR10 videos without HDR10+ and displays that take HDR10+ are not affected. Applies from the next video."
+msgstr ""
+
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+#. Setting label: HDR10 sent as Dolby Vision with metadata measured from the picture (core #40924)
+msgctxt "#32098"
+msgid "HDR10 as Dolby Vision, measured"
+msgstr ""
+
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+#. Setting help: HDR10 sent as Dolby Vision with metadata measured from the picture (core #40925)
+msgctxt "#32099"
+msgid "For a display that takes Dolby Vision. An HDR10 video, which has no dynamic metadata of its own, is sent as Dolby Vision with metadata that Hades measures from the picture as it plays: the peak, the average and the darkest level of each scene, and the black bars. These metadata are not the studio's: the studio made no Dolby Vision metadata for the video, and nothing of a colourist's grade (trims) is added. The picture is the same HDR10 picture. Scene cuts are found from the picture: a few are missed, a few are found where there is none, and some are found a picture late. Dolby Vision and HDR10+ videos are not affected. Applies from the next video."
+msgstr ""
diff --git a/addons/skin.estuary/language/resource.language.es_ar/strings.po b/addons/skin.estuary/language/resource.language.es_ar/strings.po
index 7456796..d8d62e5 100644
--- a/addons/skin.estuary/language/resource.language.es_ar/strings.po
+++ b/addons/skin.estuary/language/resource.language.es_ar/strings.po
@@ -2240,3 +2240,39 @@ msgstr "hecho de los metadatos HDR10+"
 msgctxt "#32093"
 msgid "measured by Hades from the picture"
 msgstr "medido por Hades en la imagen"
+
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+#. Setting label: Dolby Vision without its trims (core #40920)
+msgctxt "#32094"
+msgid "Dolby Vision: leave out the trims"
+msgstr "Dolby Vision: omitir los trims"
+
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+#. Setting help: Dolby Vision without its trims (core #40921)
+msgctxt "#32095"
+msgid "Dolby Vision metadata carries the trims of the film: how the colourist mapped each scene to displays of a few given peak brightnesses (levels 2 and 8 of the metadata). The display is sent them unless this is on. Turn it on only for a display that shows Dolby Vision with washed-out blacks or wrong colours because of them, as some projectors do: it then maps each scene from its brightness range alone, as it does with metadata that has no trims. The picture that is sent does not change. Applies from the next video."
+msgstr "Los metadatos Dolby Vision llevan los trims de la película: cómo el colorista ajustó cada escena para pantallas de unos pocos brillos máximos dados (los niveles 2 y 8 de los metadatos). La pantalla los recibe salvo que esto esté activado. Activalo solo para una pantalla que muestre Dolby Vision con negros lavados o colores equivocados por su causa, como hacen algunos proyectores: entonces ajusta cada escena solo a partir de su rango de brillo, como hace con metadatos sin trims. La imagen que se envía no cambia. Se aplica desde el siguiente video."
+
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+#. Setting label: HDR10+ sent as Dolby Vision (core #40922)
+msgctxt "#32096"
+msgid "HDR10+ as Dolby Vision"
+msgstr "HDR10+ como Dolby Vision"
+
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+#. Setting help: HDR10+ sent as Dolby Vision (core #40923)
+msgctxt "#32097"
+msgid "For a display that takes Dolby Vision but not HDR10+. An HDR10+ video is sent as Dolby Vision, with metadata made from its own HDR10+ metadata, scene by scene: the peak and the average brightness of each scene. The picture is the same HDR10 picture. What does not carry over from HDR10+: the tone curve and the target display that the studio chose, its saturation weight and its windows; the darkest level is taken as black, and the average is worked out from the brightness distribution that HDR10+ gives. Dolby Vision videos, HDR10 videos without HDR10+ and displays that take HDR10+ are not affected. Applies from the next video."
+msgstr "Para una pantalla que admite Dolby Vision pero no HDR10+. Un video HDR10+ se envía como Dolby Vision, con metadatos hechos de sus propios metadatos HDR10+, escena por escena: el brillo máximo y el brillo medio de cada escena. La imagen es la misma imagen HDR10. Lo que no pasa de HDR10+: la curva de tonos y la pantalla de destino que eligió el estudio, su peso de saturación y sus ventanas; el nivel más oscuro se toma como negro, y el brillo medio se calcula a partir de la distribución de brillo que da HDR10+. No afecta a los videos Dolby Vision, a los videos HDR10 sin HDR10+ ni a las pantallas que admiten HDR10+. Se aplica desde el siguiente video."
+
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+#. Setting label: HDR10 sent as Dolby Vision with metadata measured from the picture (core #40924)
+msgctxt "#32098"
+msgid "HDR10 as Dolby Vision, measured"
+msgstr "HDR10 como Dolby Vision, medido"
+
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+#. Setting help: HDR10 sent as Dolby Vision with metadata measured from the picture (core #40925)
+msgctxt "#32099"
+msgid "For a display that takes Dolby Vision. An HDR10 video, which has no dynamic metadata of its own, is sent as Dolby Vision with metadata that Hades measures from the picture as it plays: the peak, the average and the darkest level of each scene, and the black bars. These metadata are not the studio's: the studio made no Dolby Vision metadata for the video, and nothing of a colourist's grade (trims) is added. The picture is the same HDR10 picture. Scene cuts are found from the picture: a few are missed, a few are found where there is none, and some are found a picture late. Dolby Vision and HDR10+ videos are not affected. Applies from the next video."
+msgstr "Para una pantalla que admite Dolby Vision. Un video HDR10, que no tiene metadatos dinámicos propios, se envía como Dolby Vision con metadatos que Hades mide en la imagen mientras se reproduce: el brillo máximo, el brillo medio y el nivel más oscuro de cada escena, y las bandas negras. Estos metadatos no son del estudio: el estudio no hizo metadatos Dolby Vision para el video, y no se añade nada de la corrección de color de un colorista (trims). La imagen es la misma imagen HDR10. Los cortes de escena se encuentran en la imagen: unos pocos se pierden, unos pocos se encuentran donde no los hay, y algunos se encuentran una imagen tarde. No afecta a los videos Dolby Vision ni HDR10+. Se aplica desde el siguiente video."
